  "worked_solution": "At the point where $t=-1,$ the vector ${r}^{\u2032}(-1)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(-1)+u{r}^{\u2032}(-1),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-1) & =\u27e81-4(-1)^{2},5(-1)+1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-3,-4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{\u2032}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-4{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+1)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-8t,5\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ at $t=-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(-1) & =\u27e8-8(-1),5\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e88,5\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=-1$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=\u27e8-3,-4\u27e9+u\u27e88,5\u27e9,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
